From 84f11b2ceddfda5e3ef4a35b96c631665f31c704 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:18:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] epollfd_ctx: engage poll fallback when Darwin kevent rejects
 an fd with EINVAL/ENOTSUP

Old Darwin kqueues reject EVFILT_READ/EVFILT_WRITE on pty masters and
various other character devices -- with EINVAL on 10.6 up to ~10.8,
and with ENOTSUP on 10.5 -- whereas the poll-only-fd fallback
(NODE_TYPE_POLL) only engaged on ENODEV, the errno FreeBSD uses for
this. The error surfaced as an epoll_ctl failure, so terminal
emulators could not monitor their ptmx: foot on Mac OS X 10.6/PPC
opened its window but never processed any pty output (fdm.c: 'failed
to register FD=7 with epoll: Invalid argument'), and on 10.5/PPC
likewise ('failed to register FD=6 with epoll: Operation not
supported').

Accept an in-band EINVAL or ENOTSUP for NODE_TYPE_OTHER fds on Apple
as 'this device only supports poll', engaging the existing fallback.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Kvag8nXEuGz9XJL3WdSxKC
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/epollfd_ctx.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/epollfd_ctx.c b/src/epollfd_ctx.c
index 08836a4..4dbde1e 100644
--- a/src/epollfd_ctx.c
+++ b/src/epollfd_ctx.c
@@ -994,7 +994,19 @@ epollfd_ctx__register_events(EpollFDCtx *epollfd, int kq,
 
 	/* Check for fds that only support poll. */
 	if (((fd2_node->node_type == NODE_TYPE_OTHER &&
-		 kev[0].data == ENODEV) ||
+		 (kev[0].data == ENODEV
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+		     /*
+		      * Old Darwin kqueues reject pty masters and
+		      * various other character devices with EINVAL
+		      * (10.6 up to ~10.8) or ENOTSUP (10.5) rather
+		      * than ENODEV. Without this, terminal emulators
+		      * cannot monitor their ptmx: epoll_ctl fails and
+		      * input/output is never processed.
+		      */
+		     || kev[0].data == EINVAL || kev[0].data == ENOTSUP
+#endif
+		     )) ||
 		fd2_node->node_type == NODE_TYPE_POLL)) {
 
 		assert((fd2_node->events & /**/
